<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing 123 patients assessed for eligibility, with exclusions for autoimmune disease \(3\), immunodeficiency or organ transplant \(1\), tuberculosis \(1\), cancer \(1\), and insufficient data \(2\). Analysis included 115 patients, split into 90 without and 25 with postoperative ICU treatment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Composite graphic displaying five panels labeled A through E. Panel A presents a nomogram illustrating the scoring of ASA and PNI variables to estimate event risk. Panel B shows a calibration plot comparing predicted and observed event probabilities for PNI+ASA \(blue\), ASA \(red\), and PNI \(yellow\). Panel C features a decision curve analysis with net benefit plotted against risk threshold for four models, including a reference line. Panel D is a receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve with three colored lines and area under the curve \(AUC\) values; PNI+ASA outperforms individual predictors. Panel E displays horizontal color bars for PNI, ASA, and risk of event with respective scales and a color legend.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Forest plot illustrating subgroup analyses for various clinical variables, showing odds ratios with 95 percent confidence intervals and p-values for interaction. Each row displays a subgroup, corresponding event percentages, and effect estimates, with blue dots and horizontal lines representing point estimates and confidence intervals.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
